From f820ce16df563848a7e856cab50806672326dcc2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:57:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/12] Round 6: Trace SIR candidates through the prepared
 projection

Unmonitored traced SIR candidates now use the prepared projection too. In
trace mode it records every snapshot field the vendored solver records,
and the domain assembles the crn_craft::fsp::FspResult with states in
discovery order, uniformization rate, edge count, work and document
hashes. Preparation also mirrors the solver's output-reservation and
workspace checks. A unit test compares the serialized prepared result with
the vendored solver's byte for byte over the projection grid, and the
record test now includes traced candidates against the forced vendored
path. validate.py passed against the release CLI.

Workload: trace (12 traced SIR candidates, full records), 11 samples.
Before median: 2.308 ms. After median: 1.237 ms. Speedup: 1.87x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
